+### 2350 — SSH profile and credential tests are fake-only and bounded (TASK-260715-3cv3r4)
+- FINDING: The pre-existing macOS credential suite obtained a real system-domain Keychain handle for every fake-client test and created, wrote, queried, and deleted throwaway Keychains in one boundary test. That violated this task's binding fake-only execution boundary even though no production credential was used.
+- FIX: `MacOSSystemKeychainHandle` now has an inert internal fixture identity accepted only by injected fake Security clients; the live client rejects fixture handles before its injectable matcher, and a spy proves zero `SecItemCopyMatching` reachability. The suite no longer calls any live Security API and asserts one exact scoped reference query, no enumeration/fallback, malformed-reference zero calls, cancellation cleanup, passphrase states, and 16 bounded secret-lifecycle repetitions.
+- VERIFICATION: Six focused fake-only Swift suites passed 53 tests. The real coordinator boundary rejects every invalid profile class before injected Keychain/network fakes; all nine `SSHHostKeyDecision` cases traverse the candidate-neutral transport seam with `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication` only on accepted paths. Gated cancellation observes one active fake task, connection, observer, and callback before cancellation and restores the full zero baseline after success, rejection, and cancellation across 16 repetitions. Three additional cleanup/redaction matrix repetitions passed; captured-log prohibited-data, test-source live-Security, public-fixture, and live-network scans returned no matches. Coverage reported 87.75% affected lines and 87.04% affected functions; strict Swift format, core boundaries, and diff checks exited 0. No real Keychain, SSH connection, NetworkExtension runtime, VPN configuration, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.

